# No line-ending conversion anywhere: pack manifests, baselines and `git apply --3way` all hash the bytes on disk,
# and Git for Windows' autocrlf default would make the worktree differ from the blobs.
* -text
# Shell hooks must be LF on every platform (sh on Mac and Linux rejects CRLF); the whole tree is kept LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The logs are append-only entry lists (PROTOCOL.md section 2): when two clones add entries to the same spot, keep both.
# Git's built-in union driver does that with no tooling; `evergreen.py lint` then reports any duplicate ID to renumber.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
RESEARCH.md merge=union
LEARNINGS.md merge=union
TESTS.md merge=union
profile/CHANGELOG.md merge=union
profile/LEARNINGS.md merge=union
